│ patch_name               │ add_shared_crz_and_zzz_motifs                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce two motif-inspired modifications to the ansatz block to improve learning of     │
│                          │ tic-tac-toe structure while keeping parameter growth modest:                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Replace the fixed CZ entanglers with a shared-parameter CRZ ("crz_edge") on every      │
│                          │ allowed grid edge. This makes the entangling strength trainable but parameter-efficient   │
│                          │ because all edges reuse the same parameter within a block.                                │
│                          │ 2. Add collective three-qubit ZZZ rotations on the eight winning lines using a single     │
│                          │ shared parameter ("zzz_shared") per block. These explicitly target the triple             │
│                          │ correlations that define win conditions, again using sharing to keep the parameter count  │
│                          │ low.                                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Both motifs are repeated per block (and still receive independent copies across           │
│                          │ uploads/repeats), so the circuit can adapt entanglement strength and emphasize            │
│                          │ winning-line correlations while only modestly increasing N_PARAMS. The change respects    │
│                          │ connectivity and gate vocabulary constraints.                                             │
