│                          │ to emphasize center-edge control correlations (important in gameplay).                    │
│                          │ - Reduce per-block parameter count by removing many independent pre/post RZs and          │
│                          │ replacing them with two shared single-qubit RZ parameters ("rz_shared" and "rz_final")    │
│                          │ that act uniformly across qubits. This reduces N_PARAMS while preserving expressivity via │
│                          │ shared global phases.                                                                     │
│                          │ - Keep independent RY per qubit to preserve local single-qubit expressivity where needed. │
│                          │ - Maintain the CZ entangling lattice (all grid edges) to preserve connectivity and        │
│                          │ mixing.                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Parameter sharing (single rz_shared, crz_center, zzz_line, rz_final) encourages motif   │
│                          │ alignment, reduces overfitting risk, and increases parameter efficiency, which should     │
│                          │ help both test accuracy and generalization.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new block lowers N_PARAMS per block (from 27 to 13), halving total parameters while   │
│                          │ adding explicit motif-targeted triple interactions. This aims to improve test accuracy    │
