│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ winning_line_ccrz_and_local_mixing                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The previous iteration used `ZZZ` (MultiRZ) to capture winning line correlations, which   │
│                          │ improved parameter efficiency but didn't significantly boost accuracy. This edit          │
│                          │ introduces `CCRZ` (doubly-controlled RZ) gates targeting the center qubit (8) and         │
│                          │ corners, conditioned on winning line completions. This mimics a "logical AND" for board   │
│                          │ patterns.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, I am replacing the fixed `CZ` grid with `CRZ` gates. While `CZ` is a strong │
│                          │ entangler, `CRZ` allows the optimizer to tune the strength of the grid-based              │
│                          │ correlations. I also add a final `RX` layer to provide local mixing in a different basis  │
│                          │ before measurement, which is a common technique in variational circuits to increase       │
│                          │ expressivity.                                                                             │
