│                          │ phases improve detection of those less-central patterns (as suggested).                   │
│                          │ - Sharing a single zzz parameter across most winning lines biases the circuit to look for │
│                          │ three-in-a-row correlations while keeping total parameter count modest.                   │
│                          │ - Splitting CRZ into vertical/horizontal shared params allows mild asymmetry (helpful for │
│                          │ board topology) without exploding parameter count.                                        │
│                          │ Expected effect: improves representational alignment to tic-tac-toe winning triples while │
