│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_ccrz_center_controlled_triples                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce doubly-controlled RZ (CCRZ) interactions that target the center qubit           │
│                          │ conditioned on the two outer qubits of each winning line that passes through the center.  │
│                          │ Concretely, add four CCRZ gates (one per center-containing winning line) that share a     │
│                          │ single parameter "ccrz_center".  This implements a low-parameter, geometry-aligned        │
│                          │ three-qubit conditional phase intended to strengthen the circuit's sensitivity to         │
│                          │ three-in-a-row patterns involving the center (the high-leverage triples).  The change is  │
│                          │ minimally invasive (one extra parameter per block) but adds targeted non-linear capacity  │
│                          │ that often improves validation/test accuracy and reduces the train-test gap for this      │
│                          │ tic-tac-toe classification task.                                                          │
