│ patch_name               │ ccrz_and_crx_spokes_with_orientation_split                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Add lightweight parametric mixing on the center "spokes" (CRX) and introduce              │
│                          │ orientation-specific doubly-controlled RZ (CCRZ) gates across all eight winning lines.    │
│                          │ The CCRZ gates act as conditional rotations that target the middle cell of each line      │
│                          │ (controls = endpoints, target = middle), using three orientation-specific parameters      │
│                          │ (row/col/diag). This preserves symmetry-sharing within orientations while giving the      │
│                          │ circuit more expressive, motif-sensitive nonlocal interactions to detect three-in-a-row   │
│                          │ patterns. CRX on the center spokes complements the existing CRZ spokes by introducing     │
│                          │ amplitude mixing conditioned on the center, improving trainability. Parameter sharing is  │
│                          │ used deliberately (one crx_spoke, three ccrz_* keys) to keep per-block parameter count    │
│                          │ modest while increasing targeted expressive power for motif discovery.                    │
