                        Patch Metadata - Gen 25/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ zz_split_rowcoldiag_motif                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Increase expressive, domain-aligned three-qubit motifs while keeping per-block          │
│                          │ parameters moderate by splitting the previous single shared ZZZ parameter into three      │
│                          │ targeted keys: zzz_row, zzz_col, and zzz_diag. This gives the circuit flexibility to      │
│                          │ treat horizontal, vertical and diagonal winning triples differently, which should help    │
│                          │ line detection and class separation.                                                      │
│                          │ - Preserve the stable CZ lattice backbone for information propagation and keep            │
│                          │ lightweight symmetry-grouped local rotations (pre/post RZ and RY) to regularize and       │
│                          │ reduce overfitting.                                                                       │
│                          │ - Keep a single shared CRZ coupling from center to edges (crz_center_edge) to let the     │
│                          │ center modulate surrounding qubits while remaining parameter-efficient.                   │
│                          │ - Add a separate CCRZ for diagonals (ccrz_diag) to provide controlled diagonal-phase      │
│                          │ sensitivity.                                                                              │
│                          │ - Target parameter budget per block to a moderate level (14 parameters per block), giving │
│                          │ an overall parameter count that balances expressivity and trainability across the         │
│                          │ repeated / re-uploaded blocks.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvement mechanisms:                                                          │
│                          │ - Splitting ZZZ into row/col/diag allows the optimizer to emphasize features useful for   │
│                          │ different winning patterns rather than force all lines to use the same phase.             │
│                          │ - CCRZ on diagonals complements ZZZ diagonal rotations, giving a complementary            │
│                          │ controlled-phase mechanism for diagonals (helps discriminate diagonal wins).              │
│                          │ - Maintaining symmetry-grouped local rotations preserves inductive bias for the board     │
│                          │ geometry while keeping parameter count small to reduce overfitting and improve            │
│                          │ generalization.                                                                           │
│                          │ - The CZ lattice keeps entanglement capacity high without excessive additional            │
│                          │ parameters.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Hyperparameters and training-related choices remain unchanged (Adam stepsize, epochs,     │
│                          │ early stopping). The ansatz changes are confined to ANSATZ_SPEC.                          │
