│ patch_description        │ Key design changes:                                                                       │
│                          │ - Strong symmetry-based parameter sharing: corners, edges, and center share separate      │
│                          │ parameters for pre/post RZ and RY. This reduces per-block parameter count and enforces    │
│                          │ inductive biases matching the board symmetry, improving generalization and parameter      │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
│                          │ - Targeted center-edge coupling: a single shared CRZ on all center-edge links captures    │
│                          │ center-vs-edge Z-phase correlations compactly across the board.                           │
│                          │ - Motif-discovery compromise: keep a single shared ZZZ parameter for the six orthogonal   │
│                          │ winning lines (rows/cols) to capture triple correlations, but replace the two diagonal    │
│                          │ ZZZs with a shared doubly-controlled RZ (CCRZ) motif. CCRZs are parameter-efficient ways  │
│                          │ to capture diagonal triple correlations while avoiding extra costly MultiRZ parameters.   │
│                          │ - Keep the CZ lattice backbone for stable entanglement and the same data / training       │
│                          │ protocol. The resulting block has fewer unique parameters than the previous (72 total     │
│                          │ parameters vs 150), which should reduce overfitting, improve parameter efficiency, and    │
│                          │ retain targeted triple-line motifs.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Relevant parameters (externally controllable via environment or run_experiment):          │
│                          │ - learning_rate: unchanged default 0.03 (Adam stepsize).                                  │
│                          │ - n_epochs, steps_per_epoch, batch_size, early stopping patience, and convergence         │
│                          │ threshold are unchanged (controlled by run_experiment/env).                               │
│                          │ - This ansatz lowers N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK to 12 -> N_PARAMS = 12 * N_UPLOADS * N_REPEATS =  │
│                          │ 72, improving parameter efficiency and reducing generalization gap.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale: sharing enforces useful symmetry while still allowing expressive               │
│                          │ three-qubit/controlled rotations targeted at winning lines. Replacing diagonal ZZZs with  │
│                          │ a shared CCRZ reduces parameter count and tests whether controlled-RZ captures diagonal   │
│                          │ triple correlations efficiently.                                                          │
