│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ crossover_motif_ccrz_crx_shared_rz                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This program performs a careful crossover between the two provided ansatz designs to      │
│                          │ combine motif-focused three-qubit interactions with efficient parameter sharing and a     │
│                          │ touch of extra local expressivity.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Design decisions and rationale:                                                           │
│                          │ - Preserve the winning-line ZZZ motif (zzz_line) to bias the circuit toward               │
│                          │ three-in-a-row patterns (motif discovery).                                                │
│                          │ - Replace the bottom and right winning-line ZZZs with shared doubly-controlled RZs (CCRZ) │
│                          │ to probe selective controlled-phase effects while keeping parameter count low (shared     │
│                          │ "ccrz_side").                                                                             │
│                          │ - Retain the CZ lattice backbone and shared CRZ center-edge couplings (crz_center_edge)   │
│                          │ from the better-performing candidate for stable entanglement and center-edge interaction. │
│                          │ - Reuse symmetry-sharing for RZ and RY across corner/edge/center groups to keep parameter │
│                          │ efficiency and encourage rotational symmetry in the learned solution.                     │
│                          │ - Add a single global RX ("rx_global") applied to all qubits to increase local-axis       │
│                          │ expressivity without expanding the parameter set excessively.                             │
│                          │ - Add a shared CRX on two opposite center-edge pairs ("crx_center_edge") to provide       │
│                          │ additional controlled-X flexibility at low parameter cost.                                │
│                          │ - Crucially, pre- and post-entangling RZs reuse the same parameter keys per symmetry      │
│                          │ group (rz_corner, rz_edge, rz_center) to limit parameter growth while preserving depth.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Parameter accounting:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Unique per-block keys: rz_corner, rz_edge, rz_center, rx_global, ry_corner, ry_edge,    │
│                          │ ry_center, crz_center_edge, crx_center_edge, zzz_line, ccrz_side (11 keys)                │
│                          │ - With N_UPLOADS=3 and N_REPEATS=2, total parameters = 11 * 3 * 2 = 66 (matching the      │
│                          │ favorable prior candidate) while introducing the CCRZ+CRX motif combination.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The rest of the program is unchanged; only the EVOLVE-BLOCK's ANSATZ_SPEC was modified.   │
