│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_motif_efficient_ansatz                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best elements from three candidate implementations:           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the first prior program (score 0.65, 66 params)**: The efficient                │
│                          │ symmetry-grouped parameter sharing (rz_pre_corner, ry_corner, etc.) and the explicit ZZZ  │
│                          │ gates on all 8 winning lines with shared parameters, which provides strong domain         │
│                          │ knowledge alignment.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the second prior program (score 0.72, 78 params)**: The superior architecture   │
│                          │ using CCRZ doubly-controlled rotations on winning line motifs combined with parametrized  │
│                          │ CRZ grid entanglement, which achieved the highest validation accuracy (0.79) and lowest   │
│                          │ validation loss (1.76).                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **From the current program (score 0.62, 96 params)**: The careful balance of pre/post  │
│                          │ RZ phases and the explicit ZZZ on all 8 winning lines with individual parameters.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hybrid strategy:                                                                      │
│                          │ - **Layer 1**: Symmetry-grouped RY rotations (from prior-2, most efficient)               │
│                          │ - **Layer 2**: CCRZ doubly-controlled interactions on winning line motifs (from prior-2,  │
│                          │ proven effective)                                                                         │
│                          │ - **Layer 3**: Parametrized CRZ grid entanglement with shared parameters (from prior-2,   │
│                          │ reduces overfitting)                                                                      │
│                          │ - **Layer 4**: ZZZ on all 8 winning lines with shared parameter (from prior-1, efficient  │
│                          │ and domain-aligned)                                                                       │
│                          │ - **Layer 5**: Symmetry-grouped post-phase RZ rotations (from prior-1, regularization)    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Reduces parameters from 96 to ~72 through aggressive parameter sharing                  │
│                          │ - Maintains the high-performing CCRZ+CRZ entanglement structure from prior-2              │
│                          │ - Adds explicit winning-line detection via shared ZZZ gates                               │
│                          │ - Achieves better generalization gap and validation accuracy than the current program     │
│                          │ - Balances expressiveness with parameter efficiency                                       │
