│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ zzz_backbone_with_symmetry_phases                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce symmetry-grouped pre/post RZ phases (corners/edges/center), keep shared RY      │
│                          │ rotations, restore a fixed CZ lattice for robust short-range entanglement, add two shared │
│                          │ CRZ parameters for the two orthogonal edge–center axis pairs, and place targeted ZZZ      │
│                          │ three-qubit motif rotations on the eight winning lines with separate parameters for       │
│                          │ horizontal/vertical/diagonal lines.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale:                                                                                │
│                          │ - The explicit pre/post RZ degrees of freedom let each block adjust local phases before   │
│                          │ and after entangling layers, increasing expressivity without exploding parameter count.   │
│                          │ - The fixed CZ backbone stabilizes short-range correlations (low variance entangling      │
│                          │ backbone).                                                                                │
│                          │ - Parametrized CRZ center-edge couplings with two symmetry-aware keys let the circuit     │
│                          │ learn different center-edge interactions along orthogonal axes while remaining            │
│                          │ parameter-efficient.                                                                      │
│                          │ - ZZZ motifs aligned to winning lines provide inductive bias for three-in-a-row structure │
│                          │ (motif-discovery), with distinct parameters per orientation so the model can represent    │
│                          │ orientation-specific signatures.                                                          │
│                          │ This combination preserves locality constraints, uses parameters efficiently, and is      │
│                          │ designed to improve validation/test accuracy and generalization.                          │
