│ patch_name               │ add_zzz_motifs_shared_params                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Augment the existing CCRZ "winning-line" motif with collective three-qubit ZZZ rotations  │
│                          │ placed on the eight tic-tac-toe winning lines. To avoid increasing the per-block          │
│                          │ parameter count I reuse the existing CCRZ parameter names ("ccrz_line" and "ccrz_center") │
│                          │ so the new collective rotations are parameter-shared with the already-present             │
│                          │ line-conditioned rotations. This injects an additional, symmetry-aligned nonlinear        │
│                          │ observable (MultiRZ on triplets) that is well suited to detecting three-in-a-row patterns │
│                          │ while remaining parameter-efficient. I place the ZZZ motifs right after the CCRZ layer so │
│                          │ they can act together with the conditional rotations before the grid CRZs and the final   │
│                          │ local rotations.                                                                          │
