│ patch_name               │ ccrz_plus_crx_center_edge                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the motif-discovery ZZZ triples with oriented doubly-controlled RZ (CCRZ)         │
│                          │ interactions aligned to the eight winning lines, and augment the center↔edge links by     │
│                          │ adding lightweight CRX entanglers (shared parameter) in addition to the existing CRZ      │
│                          │ controls. Rationale: prior candidates that used CCRZ-style winning-line motifs plus       │
│                          │ diversified two-qubit entanglers performed better than the ZZZ-only variant. CCRZs        │
│                          │ provide directional, motif-aligned three-body phase interactions that directly target     │
│                          │ winning-line correlations, while CRX on center-edge pairs adds X-basis two-qubit          │
│                          │ correlations (complementary to CRZ) without violating grid connectivity and with only one │
│                          │ extra shared parameter. Keeping the CZ backbone and symmetry-shared single-qubit          │
│                          │ rotations preserves stable entanglement and parameter efficiency.                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
