│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ orientation_ccrz_with_line_triples                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce orientation-specific doubly-controlled RZ (CCRZ) motifs aligned with the eight  │
│                          │ winning lines (horizontal/vertical/diagonal), while keeping the ZZZ winning-line MultiRZ  │
│                          │ motifs split by orientation. Preserve a CZ lattice backbone and a single shared           │
│                          │ center-edge controlled-phase (CRZ) to focus center modulation. Use symmetry-grouped       │
│                          │ pre/post RZ and RY rotations (corner/edge/center) for parameter efficiency. This follows  │
│                          │ the motif-discovery recommendation to subdivide the CCRZ "line" parameter into            │
│                          │ orientation-specific parameters (ccrz_h, ccrz_v, ccrz_d), enabling the circuit to         │
│                          │ differentially weight horizontal, vertical and diagonal correlations with only a modest   │
│                          │ parameter increase. The resulting block uses 14 unique parameters per block (balanced     │
│                          │ expressivity + efficiency) and should improve line-detection structure and                │
│                          │ generalization.                                                                           │
