├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the original ansatz block with a motif-aware, parameter-efficient block that:     │
│                          │ - Keeps symmetry-grouped single-qubit rotations (RY and post RZ) to reduce parameter      │
│                          │ count and encourage translation symmetry.                                                 │
│                          │ - Replaces the fixed CZ backbone with trainable CRZ couplings on the ring and separate    │
│                          │ trainable CRZs to the center. This lets the optimizer tune entangling strength rather     │
│                          │ than fixing it.                                                                           │
│                          │ - Splits three-qubit ZZZ motifs into row/column/diagonal shared parameters so the circuit │
│                          │ can detect line-like patterns with fewer parameters.                                      │
│                          │ - Splits doubly-controlled RZ (CCRZ) center-involving triples into two parameter types:   │
│                          │ ccrz_edge_center (edge–edge–center triples) and ccrz_diag_center (corner–corner–center    │
│                          │ triples). This follows the suggested motif split and tests different geometry-dependent   │
│                          │ line weights without blowing up parameter count.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The block intentionally removes the pre-RZ layer (keeping only post-RZ) to reduce         │
│                          │ parameters. The resulting block uses 13 unique parameter keys -> 13 * N_UPLOADS(3) *      │
│                          │ N_REPEATS(2) = 78 total parameters, matching a well-performing prior variant while adding │
│                          │ targeted motif structure (row/col/diag ZZZ + split CCRZ). This balances expressivity,     │
│                          │ motif specificity, and parameter efficiency to improve validation/test accuracy and       │
│                          │ reduce generalization gap.                                                                │
