│ patch_name               │ symmetry_triples_plus_center_crx                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current ansatz block with a symmetry-aware, line-motif-focused block that     │
│                          │ merges the best elements seen in prior candidates: (1) explicit three-qubit ZZZ motifs    │
│                          │ aligned with the eight winning lines so the circuit can directly sense line correlations, │
│                          │ (2) a CZ lattice backbone for stable entanglement propagation, (3) shared center-edge     │
│                          │ parametric control both in Z (CRZ) and X (CRX) to give complementary phase and bit-flip   │
│                          │ controlled interactions around the important center, and (4) symmetry-grouped             │
│                          │ single-qubit rotations (pre/post RZ and RY) to reduce parameter count while retaining     │
│                          │ expressivity. A doubly-controlled diagonal CCRZ is kept to complement diagonal detection. │
│                          │ Parameter-sharing is used deliberately (corner/edge/center groups and shared center-edge  │
│                          │ controls) to keep parameter efficiency reasonable while increasing expressivity relative  │
│                          │ to the current block. This balances inductive bias toward Tic-Tac-Toe winning lines with  │
│                          │ richer control axes (CRX + CRZ) to help the optimizer reach better minima and reduce the  │
│                          │ train-test gap.                                                                           │
