│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_zzz_ccrz_backbone                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current ansatz block with a compact, symmetry-aware motif architecture that   │
│                          │ proved effective in earlier experiments.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Changes:                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Split the three-qubit ZZZ motif into separate row/column/diagonal parameters so the     │
│                          │ circuit can learn distinct responses for different geometric winning patterns.            │
│                          │ - Keep symmetry-grouped local rotations (pre/post RZ and RY) to reduce parameter count    │
│                          │ while respecting board symmetries.                                                        │
│                          │ - Retain a CZ lattice backbone for stable entanglement propagation.                       │
│                          │ - Add a shared CRZ for center-edge couplings and a CCRZ on diagonals to provide targeted  │
│                          │ center/diagonal modulation.                                                               │
│                          │ - The design uses 14 unique parameter keys per block (14 * 3 uploads * 2 repeats = 84     │
│                          │ total parameters), balancing expressivity and parameter efficiency.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale:                                                                                │
│                          │ Splitting the ZZZ motifs by geometric class encourages the circuit to develop distinct    │
│                          │ detectors for win-lines (rows, columns, diagonals). The CZ backbone ensures good          │
│                          │ entanglement spread; targeted controlled-phase gates (CRZ/CCRZ) give the network tunable  │
│                          │ interactions that focus on center-mediated and diagonal features. Grouped single-qubit    │
│                          │ rotations reduce redundant parameters while preserving symmetry priors. This              │
│                          │ configuration previously improved validation/test metrics relative to the current block.  │
