│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ symmetry_concise_zzz_center_rx                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Inspired by earlier motif-discovery candidates that placed three-qubit ZZZ motifs on the  │
│                          │ eight winning lines and symmetry-grouped single-qubit rotations, this design streamlines  │
│                          │ the ansatz to improve parameter efficiency and generalization. Key changes:               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Remove the pre-entangling RZ layer to reduce parameter count and discourage overfitting │
│                          │ (keeps lightweight local RY and a shared post-RZ).                                        │
│                          │ - Consolidate the center-edge controlled-phase into a single shared CRZ parameter         │
│                          │ (crz_center_edge) across all four center edges to respect rotational symmetry while       │
│                          │ cutting parameters.                                                                       │
│                          │ - Keep ZZZ motifs aligned to horizontal/vertical/diagonal winning lines (zzz_h, zzz_v,    │
│                          │ zzz_d) — these are expressive, physically meaningful motifs for motif-discovery.          │
│                          │ - Add a single RX on the center qubit (rx_center) to give an explicit handle for "draw"   │
│                          │ detection without blowing up parameter count.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Together these changes drop the per-block parameter count substantially (from 14 -> 11),  │
│                          │ reducing total parameters and gate depth while retaining geometric motif expressivity.    │
│                          │ This should improve validation/test generalization, lower L2 loss, and speed training     │
│                          │ convergence.                                                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
