│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ introduce_ccrz_line_motif_and_rx_rz_symmetry_grouping                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current ansatz block with a motif-aware block that previously showed strong   │
│                          │ performance: symmetry-grouped single-qubit rotations (RY, RZ, RX) to preserve geometric   │
│                          │ inductive bias, CCRZ motifs aligned with winning lines to expose three-qubit line         │
│                          │ structure, and a parameterized CRZ grid with a separate center coupling. The design       │
│                          │ deliberately keeps parameter sharing by symmetry (corners / edges / center) to remain     │
│                          │ parameter-efficient (13 unique params per block → 78 total parameters) while adding CCRZ  │
│                          │ line motifs and local RX/RZ flexibility that improved validation/test accuracy in prior   │
│                          │ runs. This reduces depth/gate complexity compared with the current CZ-heavy backbone and  │
│                          │ targets the tic-tac-toe line structure directly to improve generalization.                │
