│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ crossover_crz_zzz_motif                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This program is a crossover between the provided ansatz variants that performed best in   │
│                          │ prior runs. It keeps the fixed training loop, feature map, and measurement layout, but    │
│                          │ replaces only the EVOLVE-BLOCK ANSATZ_SPEC with a combined motif:                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Lightweight symmetry-grouped local RY rotations (corners/edges/center) to keep          │
│                          │ parameter sharing and inductive bias.                                                     │
│                          │ - A parameterized lattice entanglement layer implemented with shared CRZ gates on all     │
│                          │ grid edges (one shared "crz_grid" parameter). This replaces the fixed CZ backbone and     │
│                          │ gives the optimizer continuous control over entanglement strength while respecting        │
│                          │ adjacency constraints.                                                                    │
│                          │ - Three-qubit ZZZ motifs split by geometric category (zzz_row, zzz_col, zzz_diag) so the  │
│                          │ ansatz can specialize to rows, columns, and diagonals (motif discovery).                  │
│                          │ - Doubly-controlled CCRZ phases on the two diagonals to complement diagonal ZZZs.         │
│                          │ - Shared post-phase RZ rotations grouped by symmetry (corner/edge/center) and an          │
│                          │ additional shared RX rotation by symmetry (corner/edge/center) to increase expressivity   │
│                          │ without exploding parameter count.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The design targets the favorable expressivity/parameter-efficiency balance seen in        │
│                          │ earlier high-performing variants: 14 parameters per block, yielding 84 total parameters   │
│                          │ (with N_UPLOADS=3 and N_REPEATS=2). The choice of shared parameters and geometric         │
│                          │ splitting encourages line detection motifs while keeping parameter count moderate. Other  │
│                          │ parts of the program outside the EVOLVE-BLOCK are preserved to maintain identical         │
│                          │ inputs/outputs and training behavior.                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
