│ patch_name               │ symm_motif_compact                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This proposal keeps the paper's fixed feature map and re-uploading layout but refactors   │
│                          │ the ansatz block to be more parameter-efficient and motif-aware. It:                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Encodes geometric symmetry by grouping corner/edge/center local rotations while         │
│                          │ allowing a single shared center phase (pre/post) to reduce redundant parameters.          │
│                          │ - Preserves a CZ lattice backbone for robust short-range entanglement but augments it     │
│                          │ with targeted controlled-phase (CRZ) interactions between center and edges to focus       │
│                          │ global center modulation.                                                                 │
│                          │ - Allocates explicit three-qubit ZZZ motifs aligned with the eight winning lines          │
│                          │ (horizontal, vertical, diagonal) plus a shared doubly-controlled CCRZ diagonal phase to   │
│                          │ boost sensitivity to diagonal patterns.                                                   │
│                          │ - Reuses a small, structured set of parameters across wires where symmetry is beneficial, │
│                          │ yielding 13 parameters per block (78 total) — fewer parameters than the baseline and      │
│                          │ aligned with prior good performers — while keeping expressive three-qubit motifs to       │
│                          │ improve generalization on winning-line detection.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The block is compact (lower parameter count), structured for motif discovery (explicit    │
│                          │ ZZZ/CCRZ on win lines), and maintains the same external inputs/outputs as the original    │
│                          │ program.                                                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
