│                          │ yielded better validation/test performance. Key changes:                                  │
│                          │ - Replace fixed CZ backbone with shared-parameter CRZ couplings on every allowed grid     │
│                          │ edge (gives trainable entangling flexibility without exploding parameter count).          │
│                          │ - Keep separate shared CRZ for center–edge couplings to let center interactions differ    │
│                          │ from outer-ring edges.                                                                    │
│                          │ - Add ZZZ three-qubit motifs aligned with the six orthogonal winning lines and separate   │
│                          │ diagonal ZZZs; these explicitly encode winning-line correlations.                         │
│                          │ - Split CCRZ center interactions into edge–edge–center and corner–corner–center shared    │
│                          │ parameters to let center-conditioned phases differ by geometric category.                 │
│                          │ - Use symmetry-grouped RY (local rotations) and RZ post-phases to reduce unique           │
│                          │ parameters while preserving expressive capacity.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This mirrors the earlier high-performing ansatz (78 params total) and should improve      │
│                          │ accuracy and generalization compared to the current CZ-heavy variant.                     │
