│ patch_description        │ Replace the current lightweight, low-parameter block with a symmetry-aware motif-rich     │
│                          │ block that previously achieved stronger performance. The new ansatz restores:             │
│                          │ - grouped RY rotations by corner/edge/center for inductive bias,                          │
│                          │ - trainable CRZ couplings on outer ring edges (shared) and distinct center-edge CRZs,     │
│                          │ - explicit ZZZ three-qubit motifs aligned with the eight winning lines (separated into    │
│                          │ row/col/diag groups),                                                                     │
│                          │ - CCRZ doubly-controlled RZ interactions focused on center-involving triples              │
│                          │ (edge-edge-center and corner-corner-center),                                              │
│                          │ - grouped post-RZ rotations for phase flexibility.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This mirrors a previously successful configuration (13 unique params per block → 78 total │
│                          │ parameters given N_UPLOADS=3 and N_REPEATS=2), adding expressive three-qubit motifs that  │
│                          │ can detect winning-line correlations while keeping parameter efficiency through symmetry  │
│                          │ sharing. It keeps the existing perimeter CZ entangling structure (unchanged elsewhere)    │
│                          │ and fits connectivity/validation rules.                                                   │
