│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ motivated_line_motifs                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ I restructure the ansatz block to explicitly encode tic-tac-toe geometric motifs while    │
│                          │ keeping parameter efficiency. Key changes:                                                │
│                          │ - Replace the fixed CZ backbone with trainable CRZ entangling gates (ring vs spokes) so   │
│                          │ entanglement strengths are learned.                                                       │
│                          │ - Introduce dedicated three-qubit ZZZ motifs split by row/column/diagonal (zzz_row,       │
│                          │ zzz_col, zzz_diag) to encourage line-detection patterns.                                  │
│                          │ - Add doubly-controlled RZs (CCRZ) focused on center-involving winning lines              │
│                          │ (ccrz_center).                                                                            │
│                          │ - Use lightweight, symmetry-grouped single-qubit rotations (pre/post RZ and RY) but keep  │
│                          │ groups (corner/edge/center) to reduce parameter count and encourage inductive priors.     │
│                          │ - The block has 13 unique parameter keys -> with N_UPLOADS=3 and N_REPEATS=2 this yields  │
│                          │ 78 total tunable parameters (similar to high-performing prior candidates), balancing      │
│                          │ expressivity and efficiency.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements: the motif-aligned triples + trainable CRZ backbone should improve  │
│                          │ test/validation accuracy and reduce the train-test gap while keeping parameter efficiency │
│                          │ high.                                                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
