│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ winning_line_motif_crx_hybrid                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This ansatz evolves the previous winning-line motif strategy by introducing a hybrid      │
│                          │ entanglement layer. It combines the high-expressivity of three-qubit ZZZ interactions     │
│                          │ (aligned with all 8 winning Tic-Tac-Toe lines) with a dual-basis two-qubit entanglement   │
│                          │ layer.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. **Winning Line Priors**: Explicitly uses ZZZ gates for all 8 winning lines (rows,      │
│                          │ columns, diagonals) to capture the game's terminal logic directly in the Hilbert space.   │
│                          │ 2. **Dual-Basis Entanglement**: Replaces the static CZ backbone with a combination of     │
│                          │ fixed CZ gates and parametrized CRX gates on the grid edges. CRX provides non-commuting   │
│                          │ entanglement relative to the RX feature map and RZ/ZZZ motifs, helping the model escape   │
│                          │ local minima.                                                                             │
│                          │ 3. **Symmetry-Aware Parameter Sharing**: Groups parameters by geometric role (corners,    │
│                          │ edges, center) and orientation (horizontal, vertical, diagonal) to maintain a low         │
│                          │ parameter count (72 total) while maximizing the representational power of each degree of  │
│                          │ freedom.                                                                                  │
│                          │ 4. **Phase Balancing**: Uses a sandwich structure of RY and RZ rotations to allow the     │
│                          │ circuit to learn arbitrary single-qubit SU(2) transformations before and after the        │
│                          │ entangling motifs.                                                                        │
