│ patch_name               │ ccrz_zzz_symm                                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This candidate reintroduces the winning-line three-qubit motifs and symmetry-aware local  │
│                          │ rotations that proved effective in earlier seeds. Key design choices:                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Explicitly encodes the eight tic-tac-toe winning lines via CCRZ and ZZZ motifs so the   │
│                          │ circuit can directly learn three-in-a-row correlations.                                   │
│                          │ - Preserves paper-inspired symmetry by sharing single-qubit rotation parameters across    │
│                          │ corners, edges, and the center (parameter efficient but expressive).                      │
│                          │ - Uses parametrized CRZ couplings on the grid edges and distinct center-edge CRZs so the  │
│                          │ circuit can tune short-range and center couplings independently.                          │
│                          │ - Adds both RZ and RX symmetry-grouped rotations after entangling motifs to increase      │
│                          │ representational flexibility while keeping the number of unique parameters the same as    │
│                          │ successful prior seeds (13 keys), so N_PARAMS remains 78 with the fixed upload/repeat     │
│                          │ scheme.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These choices aim to increase test/validation accuracy and reduce the train-test gap by   │
│                          │ combining explicit three-qubit line awareness with locality-respecting entanglement and   │
│                          │ symmetry-based parameter sharing.                                                         │
