│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ interleaved_crx_entanglement                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The previous best candidate showed that grid-based CRZ entanglement and CCRZ motifs       │
│                          │ significantly improved accuracy and reduced loss. To further improve the expressivity of  │
│                          │ the entanglement layer without increasing the parameter count significantly, I am         │
│                          │ interleaving CRX gates into the grid-based entanglement layer.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By using the same `crz_grid` and `crz_to_center` parameter names for the CRX gates, we    │
│                          │ allow the circuit to perform a more complex basis-mixing operation (X and Z rotations)    │
│                          │ conditioned on the same control-target pairs. This "XY-style" entanglement can capture    │
│                          │ non-classical correlations more effectively than pure Z-basis entanglement. I am also     │
│                          │ adding a final set of RY rotations to provide a last trainable basis change before the    │
│                          │ measurements.                                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
