╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ structured_line_correlations_with_crx                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The existing ansatz uses Z-basis interactions (ZZZ, CCRZ, CRZ) heavily. While these       │
│                          │ capture board correlations, the classification task might benefit from non-diagonal       │
│                          │ interactions that better distribute information across the hilbert space for the final    │
│                          │ observables.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This change introduces:                                                                   │
│                          │ 1. `CRX` gates along the grid edges to provide a different entanglement basis compared to │
│                          │ the uniform `CRZ` ring.                                                                   │
│                          │ 2. An additional symmetry-grouped `RX` layer to allow the circuit to rotate into a more   │
│                          │ expressive basis before the final Z-measurements.                                         │
│                          │ 3. Re-organizes the `CCRZ` and `ZZZ` logic to ensure all eight winning lines are          │
│                          │ represented by `ZZZ` motifs while `CCRZ` focuses on center-correlated 'fork' patterns.    │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0191                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
