│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ orthogonal_basis_alternation                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The previous candidate successfully integrated winning-line motifs (ZZZ and CCRZ) but saw │
│                          │ a slight drop in accuracy compared to the seed. This edit introduces a more diverse       │
│                          │ interaction subspace by alternating the basis of the three-qubit motifs.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Specifically, we keep the ZZZ motifs (which capture parity-like correlations across       │
│                          │ lines) but replace the CCRZ motifs with a "line-conditioned" rotation motif using CRX/CRY │
│                          │ logic (simulated here via symmetry-grouped RX/RY layers and selective ZZZ/CRZ             │
│                          │ interactions).                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To improve expressivity without ballooning parameter count, we:                           │
│                          │ 1.  Group the ZZZ motifs by row, column, and diagonal to allow the model to weight        │
│                          │ different win-orientations differently.                                                   │
│                          │ 2.  Introduce a 'mid-block' RY layer to allow the circuit to rotate out of the Z-basis    │
│                          │ before the final entanglement, improving the non-linearity of the decision boundary.      │
│                          │ 3.  Maintain parameter efficiency by sharing keys across symmetric board positions.       │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0225                                                                                   │
