│ patch_name               │ symmetry_line_motif_crossover                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This candidate performs a crossover between the 'motif-discovery' geometric approach and  │
│                          │ the 'symmetry-grouped' parameter sharing strategy.                                        │
│                          │ 1. It retains the high-performing winning line motifs using CCRZ and ZZZ gates from the   │
│                          │ crossover program, as these directly map the win/loss logic to 3-qubit interactions.      │
│                          │ 2. It adopts the symmetry-grouped parameters (corners, edges, center) for single-qubit    │
│                          │ rotations (RY, RZ) from the primary program to maintain high parameter efficiency and     │
│                          │ regularization.                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. It optimizes the entanglement layer by using shared 'ring' and 'to_center' CRZ         │
│                          │ parameters, which proved effective in reducing the generalization gap.                    │
│                          │ 4. The post-rotation layer uses a single shared parameter for all RZ gates to reduce      │
│                          │ depth while allowing for a final phase adjustment, balancing expressivity and parameter   │
│                          │ count.                                                                                    │
│                          │ Overall, this combined strategy aims to capture the winning board patterns through        │
│                          │ higher-order motifs while keeping the local landscapes simple and symmetric.              │
