│ patch_description        │ This ansatz performs a crossover between the symmetry-grouped rotation strategy and the   │
│                          │ winning-line motif discovery strategy.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. It adopts the symmetry-grouped RY/RZ/RX rotations from the second program, which       │
│                          │ provides a robust basis for state preparation and phase management across corners, edges, │
│                          │ and the center.                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. It integrates the winning-line CCRZ motifs (Layer 2 of the second program) which       │
│                          │ specifically target the geometry of tic-tac-toe by conditioning rotations on the          │
│                          │ completion of lines.                                                                      │
│                          │ 3. It retains the ZZZ (MultiRZ) interactions from the first program, categorized by row,  │
│                          │ column, and diagonal, to capture collective parity information essential for board        │
│                          │ evaluation.                                                                               │
│                          │ 4. It uses shared parameters within these geometric groups to maintain high parameter     │
│                          │ efficiency (keeping n_params at 78) while increasing the expressive power of the circuit. │
│                          │ 5. The combination aims to reduce validation loss and improve test accuracy by aligning   │
│                          │ the circuit topology with the game's winning conditions.                                  │
