│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ crossover_symmetry_triple_mixer                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This program is a crossover of the provided candidate ansatz designs. It preserves the    │
│                          │ fixed training, data handling, and measurement logic while proposing an improved          │
│                          │ ANSATZ_SPEC inside the EVOLVE-BLOCK.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas merged:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Symmetry-sharing of single-qubit rotations (corner / edge / center) to reduce unique    │
│                          │ parameters and improve parameter efficiency (from prior designs).                         │
│                          │ - A shared RX "mixer" applied across all qubits (lightweight global mixing) to increase   │
│                          │ expressivity while keeping parameters low.                                                │
│                          │ - A trainable CRZ lattice backbone for local entanglement on the outer ring and a         │
│                          │ separate shared CRZ for center-edge couplings (so center interactions can differ from the │
│                          │ ring).                                                                                    │
│                          │ - Explicit ZZZ motifs aligned with the eight winning lines, split into                    │
│                          │ row/column/diagonal groups to capture triple correlations using few parameters            │
│                          │ (motif-discovery inspiration).                                                            │
│                          │ - Doubly-controlled RZ (CCRZ) motifs focused on diagonals (corner-corner -> center) as a  │
│                          │ parameter-efficient way to emphasize diagonal correlations.                               │
│                          │ - Shared post-RZ symmetry groups to add phase flexibility without increasing parameter    │
│                          │ count.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Parameter budget is kept comparable to the successful prior runs (13 unique parameters    │
│                          │ per block => 78 total parameters over 6 blocks) to preserve efficient training while      │
│                          │ improving representational inductive biases aligned with tic-tac-toe structure. These     │
│                          │ changes aim to improve validation/test generalization and reduce overfitting by           │
│                          │ leveraging geometry-aware motifs and parameter sharing.                                   │
