│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ remove_duplicate_center_crz                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Remove redundant center-edge CRZ entries that were duplicated twice in the block: the     │
│                          │ crz_ring backbone originally included the four center-edge links ([1,8], [3,8], [5,8],    │
│                          │ [7,8]) and the block then re-applied separate crz_center_edge gates on the same wires.    │
│                          │ This produced duplicated two-qubit gates on the same wires (increasing gate_count and     │
│                          │ depth) while adding little extra representational benefit. The edit removes the           │
│                          │ center-edge links from the crz_ring backbone so that the four center-edge CRZs appear     │
│                          │ only once (under crz_center_edge). This reduces circuit depth and gate count, removes     │
│                          │ redundant entangling that can hurt training stability/generalization, and keeps the       │
│                          │ parameterization (and therefore N_PARAMS) unchanged.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
