│ patch_name               │ geometric_motif_crx_hybrid                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This ansatz improves performance by introducing non-commuting X-basis correlations into   │
│                          │ the grid entanglement layer. While the previous version relied heavily on Z-basis         │
│                          │ interactions (CRZ, ZZZ, CCRZ), this candidate adds a shared-parameter CRX layer on the    │
│                          │ same grid edges. This allows the circuit to capture non-trivial basis transformations     │
│                          │ between the feature map (RX) and the measurement (Z), effectively increasing the          │
│                          │ expressive power of the entanglement without significantly increasing the parameter       │
│                          │ count. We also refine the symmetry grouping of the three-qubit ZZZ motifs to better       │
│                          │ distinguish between orthogonal winning lines (rows vs columns) and diagonals, which are   │
│                          │ geometrically distinct on the 9-qubit grid.                                               │
