│ patch_name               │ hybrid_symmetry_triples                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This program is a crossover that blends the strongest motifs from the prior candidates    │
│                          │ while keeping parameter efficiency high (matching the 78-parameter best). The evolved     │
│                          │ ANSATZ_SPEC (inside EVOLVE-BLOCK) uses symmetry-grouped single-qubit rotations (shared    │
│                          │ params for corners/edges/center), a parametrized CRZ ring backbone plus separate          │
│                          │ center-edge CRZs, targeted three-qubit ZZZ motifs aligned with the eight winning lines    │
│                          │ (shared by orientation), and doubly-controlled CCRZ interactions focused on               │
│                          │ center-related triples. A single shared post-RZ parameter is used to keep parameter count │
│                          │ low and encourage useful global phase flexibility. The resulting per-block unique         │
│                          │ parameter count is 13 -> 13 * N_UPLOADS(3) * N_REPEATS(2) = 78 total parameters (matching │
│                          │ the best-performing variant), while preserving useful geometric motifs (winning-line      │
│                          │ triples, center-conditioned CCRZs, ring entanglement). No changes were made outside the   │
│                          │ EVOLVE block to ensure identical inputs/outputs and to maintain the fixed                 │
│                          │ training/evaluation protocol.                                                             │
