│ patch_name               │ winning_line_ccrz_motifs                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses ZZZ (MultiRZ) for winning lines and CCRZ for center-related       │
│                          │ triples. This edit replaces the generic ZZZ motifs with CCRZ (doubly-controlled RZ) gates │
│                          │ specifically targeting the third qubit in every winning line. CCRZ is a more powerful     │
│                          │ non-linear gate for boolean-like logic (if A and B are set, rotate C), which map directly │
│                          │ to the "two-in-a-row" logic of Tic-Tac-Toe. I also simplify the parameter sharing to      │
│                          │ focus on the geometric roles (rows, columns, diagonals) and ensure the center qubit (8)   │
│                          │ is properly integrated into the line logic.                                               │
