│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ symmetry_zzz_crz_ccrz                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Reduced and structured parameterization: symmetry-grouped single-qubit rotations        │
│                          │ (corner/edge/center), shared CRZ ring and distinct center-edge CRZ, ZZZ motifs placed     │
│                          │ exactly on the eight winning lines (row/col/diag groups), CCRZ center interactions        │
│                          │ grouped by geometry, and shared post-RZ symmetry rotations. This yields 13 unique         │
│                          │ parameters per block → 13 * N_UPLOADS * N_REPEATS = 78 total parameters (compact and      │
│                          │ parameter-efficient).                                                                     │
│                          │ - Geometric motif induction: placing ZZZ on winning lines and CCRZ interactions focused   │
│                          │ on center-edge/diagonal motifs encourages the ansatz to directly learn relevant           │
│                          │ three-body correlations for tic-tac-toe outcomes, improving generalization and sample     │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
│                          │ - Heavy parameter sharing across symmetric board positions reduces overfitting (smaller   │
│                          │ train-test gap) while preserving expressive three-body and two-body entangling motifs.    │
│                          │ - Training hyperparameters are unchanged (optimizer: Adam, default LR=0.03, early         │
│                          │ stopping with patience), so the candidate benefits from better inductive bias without     │
│                          │ tuning the learning schedule.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected effect:                                                                          │
│                          │ - Lower parameter count and motif-aligned three-qubit interactions improve                │
│                          │ validation/test accuracy and reduce generalization gap compared to larger,                │
│                          │ less-structured blocks.                                                                   │
│                          │ - Parameter sharing reduces depth/gate count relative to the current program and improves │
│                          │ parameter efficiency.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Tunable parameters left for the outer training loop:                                      │
│                          │ - learning_rate (default 0.03), n_epochs (default 100), steps_per_epoch (default 30),     │
│                          │ batch_size (default 15)                                                                   │
│                          │ - early_stopping (default on), patience (default 75), min_delta (1e-4)                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This proposal keeps the same inputs/outputs and training/evaluation protocol but supplies │
│                          │ a more compact, symmetry- and motif-aware ANSATZ_SPEC.                                    │
