                        Patch Metadata - Gen 68/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sym_shared_cz_zzz_compact                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This candidate reduces parameter count and enforces a strong, geometry-aligned inductive  │
│                          │ bias to improve generalization and parameter efficiency.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Design choices:                                                                           │
│                          │ - Replace many parametrized two-qubit CRZs with fixed CZ entangling edges to keep         │
│                          │ entanglement expressive while removing tunable two-qubit parameters (reduces N_PARAMS).   │
│                          │ - Preserve symmetry grouping: corners, edges, center share RY/RZ parameters to capture    │
│                          │ geometric invariances with few parameters.                                                │
│                          │ - Introduce explicit three-qubit ZZZ motifs on every winning line. Rows/columns share one │
│                          │ parameter (zzz_line) while the two diagonals share a second (zzz_diag). This targets the  │
│                          │ game's triple correlations directly and compactly.                                        │
│                          │ - Add a single RX on the center qubit to give extra flexibility for the draw-class        │
│                          │ observable without proliferating parameters.                                              │
│                          │ - The resulting block is shallower in parameter space (fewer unique parameters per        │
│                          │ block), improving parameter efficiency and reducing overfitting risk while preserving     │
│                          │ rich entangling structure via CZ + ZZZ motifs.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected outcome:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Fewer total trainable parameters (54 vs 78 previously) -> better parameter efficiency.  │
│                          │ - Explicit winning-line ZZZ motifs to improve accuracy on line-detection tasks.           │
