│ patch_name               │ motif_symmetry_crossover                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover returns a refined ansatz that blends the stronger motif-aware design from  │
│                          │ the best prior program with the stable training/utility scaffolding of the current        │
│                          │ program. Key choices:                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Use symmetry-grouped single-qubit rotations (corners, edges, center) to improve         │
│                          │ parameter efficiency and inductive bias.                                                  │
│                          │ - Include shared CRZ couplings around the outer ring and separate center-edge CRZ         │
│                          │ couplings, giving expressible but compact entanglement.                                   │
│                          │ - Add ZZZ multi-qubit rotations aligned to the eight winning lines, grouped by geometric  │
│                          │ orientation (rows/cols/diagonals) to enable motif discovery aligned with the task.        │
│                          │ - Split CCRZ center-conditioned triples by geometry (edge-edge-center vs                  │
│                          │ corner-corner-center) to allow different center-conditioning behaviors.                   │
│                          │ - Restore separate post-RZ phase parameters per symmetry group (corner/edge/center) for   │
│                          │ flexibility without exploding parameter count.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This ANSATZ_SPEC matches the high-performing motif-discovery variant from prior           │
│                          │ experiments (keeps N_PARAMS_per_block = 13), and is dropped into the unchanged            │
│                          │ training/evaluation framework for consistent comparison.                                  │
