│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ perimeter_spoke_zzz_ccrz                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Reduce parameter count per block to 13 (78 total) by exploiting tic-tac-toe symmetries: │
│                          │ corners share, edges share, center treated separately. This improves parameter efficiency │
│                          │ and reduces overfitting.                                                                  │
│                          │ - Split grid CRZ couplings into two shared parameters: crz_ring for the eight outer-ring  │
│                          │ edges and crz_center_edge for the four spokes to the center. This gives the optimizer     │
│                          │ explicit control over perimeter vs hub correlations.                                      │
│                          │ - Include ZZZ (three-qubit) rotations aligned with the eight winning lines (rows,         │
│                          │ columns, diagonals) grouped into three shared parameters (row/col/diag) to directly       │
│                          │ encode higher-order motifs relevant to the task.                                          │
│                          │ - Use CCRZ (doubly-controlled RZ) interactions split by geometry (edge-edge-center vs     │
│                          │ corner-corner-center) to provide additional expressive, motif-aligned nonlinearity at low │
│                          │ parameter cost.                                                                           │
│                          │ - Finish with symmetry-grouped RZ rotations to allow final phase adjustments.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This configuration mirrors the best prior seed (78 params) but emphasizes the             │
│                          │ perimeter/spoke CRZ split and motif-aligned triple interactions. Fewer parameters,        │
│                          │ structured sharing, and geometry-aligned three-body gates improve generalization and      │
│                          │ parameter efficiency while keeping expressivity for the tic-tac-toe classification task.  │
