│ patch_name               │ interleave_non_diagonal_between_three_body                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Insert additional single-qubit RY rotations between the Z-diagonal multi-qubit motif      │
│                          │ layer (ZZZ)                                                                               │
│                          │ and the doubly-controlled RZ layer (CCRZ). The added RY gates reuse the existing          │
│                          │ symmetry-grouped                                                                          │
│                          │ parameter keys (ry_corner, ry_edge, ry_center), so no extra trainable parameters are      │
│                          │ introduced.                                                                               │
│                          │ This breaks up long sequences of commuting Z-diagonal gates, increasing circuit           │
│                          │ expressivity and                                                                          │
│                          │ mixing while keeping parameter efficiency. The change is purely a gate-ordering /         │
│                          │ interleaving                                                                              │
│                          │ modification that is inexpensive (no new params) and aims to improve optimization and     │
│                          │ generalization.                                                                           │
