│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_repeat_zzz_ccrz                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Restructures the ANSATZ_SPEC to introduce a hybrid three-body motif strategy that keeps   │
│                          │ the 78-parameter budget while improving expressiveness. The key changes:                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Modular gate organization**: The ansatz is now organized into clear logical blocks   │
│                          │ (pre-entanglement, winning-line interactions, post-entanglement) instead of a flat list,  │
│                          │ improving readability and maintainability.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Repeat-dependent mutation**: The ansatz block is applied differently across the two  │
│                          │ repeats within each upload:                                                               │
│                          │    - **Repeat 0** (even blocks): Uses CCRZ gates on all eight winning-line triplets under │
│                          │ two shared parameters (ccrz_line and ccrz_center).                                        │
│                          │    - **Repeat 1** (odd blocks): Replaces all eight CCRZ gates with ZZZ gates on the same  │
│                          │ geometric triplets under two shared parameters (zzz_line and zzz_center).                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Preserved architecture**: Maintains the symmetric RY/RZ parametrization, grid-based  │
│                          │ CRZ couplings, and identical gate count/depth (~279 gates, ~112 depth) so candidates      │
│                          │ remain comparable.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Enhanced three-body expressiveness**: By probing both doubly-controlled RZ (CCRZ)    │
│                          │ and collective Z-basis rotation (ZZZ) on the winning lines across alternating repeats,    │
│                          │ the circuit gains richer capacity to capture non-classical correlations while respecting  │
│                          │ the 78-param constraint.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design balances parameter efficiency with increased expressiveness, enabling the     │
│                          │ circuit to learn more sophisticated board-state representations without exceeding the     │
│                          │ fixed budget.                                                                             │
