╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ winline_motif_shared                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Encode tic-tac-toe winning structure explicitly by adding CCRZ interactions on every    │
│                          │ winning line (shared parameter "ccrz_line") so the circuit can directly sense             │
│                          │ three-in-a-row correlations.                                                              │
│                          │ - Use Multi-Z (ZZZ) rotations separated into row/column vs diagonal groups ("zzz_rowcol", │
│                          │ "zzz_diag") to capture collective parity along those geometries.                          │
│                          │ - Maintain light-weight, symmetry-aware single-qubit rotations (shared corner/edge/center │
│                          │ RY and RZ) for parameter efficiency and to respect board symmetries.                      │
│                          │ - Add a single shared RX mixing rotation ("rx_shared") on every qubit to increase         │
│                          │ expressivity without exploding parameter count.                                           │
│                          │ - Keep parametrized controlled-Z couplings around the outer ring ("crz_ring") and radial  │
│                          │ couplings to center ("crz_to_center"), plus controlled-X radial couplings                 │
│                          │ ("crx_to_center") to give both phase and amplitude entangling channels.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should improve performance:                                                      │
│                          │ - Directly providing CCRZ and ZZZ motifs on the eight winning lines gives the optimizer   │
│                          │ the ability to form features aligned with the task's combinatorial structure (detecting   │
│                          │ 3-in-a-row), improving sample efficiency and classification accuracy.                     │
│                          │ - Symmetry-based parameter sharing reduces overfitting and the train-test gap while       │
│                          │ keeping expressive nonlocal interactions available (via CCRZ/ZZZ).                        │
│                          │ - Mixing both CRZ and CRX radial couplings gives complementary entangling mechanisms for  │
│                          │ center-vs-edge signals (important because center participates in many winning lines).     │
│                          │ - Overall parameter budget per block remains compact (13 keys), keeping total N_PARAMS    │
│                          │ similar to prior designs but shifting expressivity into structured multi-qubit motifs     │
│                          │ that directly match the problem geometry.                                                 │
