│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ motif_aligned_zzz_ccrz_with_compact_rotations                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the seed ansatz with a motif-aware, symmetry-compressed block that proved         │
│                          │ effective in prior variants:                                                              │
│                          │ - Keep efficient symmetry-grouped RY local rotations (corners/edges/center).              │
│                          │ - Use shared CRZ "ring" + shared CRZ center couplings for robust grid entanglement.       │
│                          │ - Replace a single shared ZZZ with geometry-aligned ZZZ motifs separated into             │
│                          │ rows/cols/diags (three parameters). This explicitly encodes the eight winning lines as    │
│                          │ collective Z rotations, making the ansatz capable of learning line-specific correlations  │
│                          │ (motif discovery).                                                                        │
│                          │ - Add CCRZ high-order correlations grouped into center and diagonal families to capture   │
│                          │ conditional three-qubit effects without exploding parameter count.                        │
│                          │ - Collapse the final single-qubit RZ+RX into a compact 'rot_*' parameter per symmetry     │
│                          │ zone (corners/edges/center). Implemented by applying RZ then RX with the same parameter   │
│                          │ name for each wire in the symmetry group. This reduces effective free-parameter           │
│                          │ complexity while retaining expressive local rotations.                                    │
│                          │ This edit keeps all gates legal under the schema/constraints and aims to improve          │
│                          │ validation/test accuracy and parameter efficiency by aligning three-qubit motifs with     │
│                          │ task structure and compressing redundant single-qubit parameters.                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
