│ patch_description        │ This program is a crossover between two high-performing candidate ansatze. It preserves   │
│                          │ the original training, data, and evaluation pipeline while improving the ansatz block by  │
│                          │ combining symmetry-aware parameter sharing, a fixed CZ backbone for stable short-range    │
│                          │ entanglement, shared controlled-RZ (CRZ) grid couplings, explicit three-qubit ZZZ motifs  │
│                          │ aligned with tic-tac-toe winning lines, and compressed CCRZ higher-order interactions.    │
│                          │ The block reduces redundant parameters via symmetry grouping (corners/edges/center) and   │
│                          │ reuses center-focused CCRZ weights to keep parameter count efficient while preserving     │
│                          │ expressive high-order motifs. The layout is ordered to encourage local entanglement then  │
│                          │ line-sensitive three-body motifs and finishes with compact post-phase rotations plus a    │
│                          │ small RX on the center to tune draw sensitivity. The EVOLVE-BLOCK markers remain intact;  │
│                          │ only ANSATZ_SPEC is changed.                                                              │
