│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ swap_zzz_early_and_parameter_compression                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Move the three-qubit ZZZ "winning-line" motifs earlier in the block (immediately after    │
│                          │ the symmetry RY layer) to encourage the circuit to form line-correlations before broader  │
│                          │ ring entanglement. At the same time reduce parameter count and encourage symmetry by      │
│                          │ merging redundant CRZ/CCRZ/RZ parameter groups:                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Share all grid CRZs (outer ring + center edges) under a single "crz_ring" parameter to  │
│                          │ compress radial vs. ring coupling into one tunable scale (reduces one parameter).         │
│                          │ - Share all CCRZ three-body controls into one "ccrz_center" parameter (reduces one        │
│                          │ parameter).                                                                               │
│                          │ - Merge post-entanglement corner+edge RZs into a single "rz_post_outer" shared parameter  │
│                          │ (reduces one parameter).                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These compressions lower N_PARAMS from 96 to 78 (improving parameter efficiency) while    │
│                          │ the earlier placement of ZZZ tests whether explicit winning-line interactions accelerate  │
│                          │ learning and tightens generalization. The wiring and gate vocabulary remain valid under   │
│                          │ connectivity rules.                                                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0158                                                                                   │
