                        Patch Metadata - Gen 81/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Insert a targeted symmetry-grouped phase layer immediately after the ZZZ winning-line     │
│                          │ motifs and rebalance parameter usage to keep the per-block parameter count unchanged      │
│                          │ (thus preserving the total N_PARAMS = 78). The phase layer adds local RZ phases on        │
│                          │ corners, edges and the center right after the line-aligned ZZZ entanglers so the ansatz   │
│                          │ can adjust relative Z-basis phases induced by those three-body interactions (a            │
│                          │ hypothesis-driven motif for tic-tac-toe pattern discrimination).                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To retain the same number of unique parameters per block we:                              │
│                          │ - Merge the center-edge CRZ parameters into the existing ring CRZ parameter ("crz_ring")  │
│                          │ so all CRZs share "crz_ring".                                                             │
│                          │ - Merge both CCRZ groups to use a single "ccrz_diag" key (compressing center/edge         │
│                          │ double-control rotations to the same compact key).                                        │
│                          │ - Collapse the final Layer5 rot parameters "rot_edges" and "rot_center" into a single     │
│                          │ "rot_others" to free one key.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Net effect: +3 new phase keys (phase_corners/phase_edges/phase_center) and -3 keys from   │
│                          │ sharing/collapsing, keeping N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK unchanged. This minimally increases        │
│                          │ expressive power near geometrically-relevant entanglers while preserving parameter        │
│                          │ efficiency and training resource profile.                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0165                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/openai/gpt-5-mini                                                              │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 12; deleted: 0; modified: 24;                                                      │
