│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ crx_mixed_motif                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Key changes and motivation:                                                               │
│                          │ - Keep the same parameter budget and re-upload/repeat layout (N_UPLOADS=3, N_REPEATS=2)   │
│                          │ so comparisons remain fair.                                                               │
│                          │ - Introduce CRX entanglers around the outer ring (shared parameter). Because the feature  │
│                          │ map uses RX rotations, adding controlled-X rotations (CRX) provides complementary X-basis │
│                          │ coupling that better mixes the encoded features before/alongside Z-basis interactions.    │
│                          │ - Add compact pre-entangling RZ phases (shared by symmetry groups) to break unwanted      │
│                          │ symmetries and give phase flexibility to the block.                                       │
│                          │ - Preserve the motif-discovery elements (ZZZ on winning lines and CCRZ triples) so the    │
│                          │ ansatz can still learn high-order correlations aligned with game-winning patterns.        │
│                          │ - Use symmetry-aware parameter sharing (corners/edges/center groups) to keep the number   │
│                          │ of independent parameters identical to previous candidates (13 per block => 78 total)     │
│                          │ while capturing geometric priors.                                                         │
│                          │ Expectations: richer cross-basis entangling (CRX + CRZ + ZZZ) and modest                  │
│                          │ symmetry-breaking phases should improve representational power, lower L2 loss, and        │
│                          │ increase validation/test accuracy without increasing overfitting or parameter count.      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
