│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ inject_symmetry_phases_and_rebalance                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This modification injects a targeted phase layer (RZ) immediately after the high-order    │
│                          │ `ZZZ` interactions to allow the circuit to better process the non-local correlations      │
│                          │ generated by the winning-line motifs. By grouping these phases by symmetry (corners,      │
│                          │ edges, center), we introduce specific degrees of freedom to adjust the interference       │
│                          │ patterns before the final rotation layer. To maintain the parameter count at 78 (13       │
│                          │ unique parameters per block), the final `RZ` and `RX` rotations for edges and center are  │
│                          │ collapsed into a single `rot_others` parameter. This trade-off tests if local phase       │
│                          │ adjustments following multi-qubit entanglement are more valuable than independent final   │
│                          │ rotation angles for non-corner qubits.                                                    │
