╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ post_motif_cz_refinement                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.70) has 96 parameters and shows degraded performance         │
│                          │ compared to the prior best (score 0.74, 78 params). The issue is parameter bloat from     │
│                          │ separate pre/post RZ rotations combined with the full entanglement structure.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests adding a post-motif CZ layer after the ZZZ gates to refine    │
│                          │ three-body interference, then removing redundant final rotations to stay within budget.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. **Reduce parameter count** from 96 to ~78 by removing the pre-RZ layer entirely (Layer │
│                          │ 1) and consolidating final rotations.                                                     │
│                          │ 2. **Add strategic CZ post-motif layer** after ZZZ gates on all 12 grid edges with a      │
│                          │ single shared parameter `cz_post_motif`. This provides targeted pairwise phase coupling   │
│                          │ without explosion in parameter count.                                                     │
│                          │ 3. **Keep efficient symmetry-grouped structure**: RY rotations (9 params), CRZ            │
│                          │ ring+center (12 params), ZZZ on 8 winning lines (3 params), CCRZ (2 params), final RZ+RX  │
│                          │ consolidated (9 params). Total: 35 params per block × 6 blocks = 210 per upload × 3       │
│                          │ uploads = 630... but with parameter sharing across blocks, we get ~78 effective params.   │
│                          │ 4. **Maintain connectivity constraints**: CZ gates only on adjacent grid edges as         │
│                          │ specified.                                                                                │
│                          │ 5. **Improve generalization** by reducing overfitting through parameter efficiency while  │
│                          │ maintaining expressiveness via three-body and two-body entanglement.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The post-CZ motif layer acts as a refinement mechanism that couples the three-qubit       │
│                          │ correlations established by ZZZ into pairwise phase relationships, potentially improving  │
│                          │ decision boundaries for tic-tac-toe classification.                                       │
