│ patch_name               │ post_motif_cz_add_and_edge_rz_prune                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Add a symmetry-grouped post-motif pairwise entangler layer of CZ gates immediately after  │
│                          │ the ZZZ motif layer to reinforce pairwise phase coupling following the three-body motifs. │
│                          │ To keep parameter and capacity budgets controlled (and reduce overfitting risk), remove   │
│                          │ the final RZ on the four edge qubits (rz_post_edge). The added CZs are fixed              │
│                          │ (non-parameterized) so they increase entangling structure without increasing the          │
│                          │ parameter count; pruning rz_post_edge reduces the per-block parameter count, improving    │
│                          │ parameter efficiency and helping generalization. This small structural change encourages  │
│                          │ motif-formed three-body interactions to be consolidated by pairwise phases along the grid │
│                          │ edges while slightly lowering N_PARAMS.                                                   │
