│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ccrz_early_symmetry_compact_block                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Move the doubly-controlled CCRZ three-qubit interactions immediately after the local RY   │
│                          │ rotations so high-order motif correlations are planted early (RY → CCRZ → CRZ → ZZZ →     │
│                          │ compact RZ+RX). This follows the motif-discovery recommendation: seed high-order          │
│                          │ correlations right after local feature rotations to accelerate learning of winning-line   │
│                          │ patterns.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Also reduce and reuse parameters by grouping rotations and entanglers by geometric        │
│                          │ symmetry (corners/edges/center, ring vs center couplings, row/col/diag ZZZ groups) to     │
│                          │ match a previously strong seed (13 unique keys, 78 total params). Fewer unique parameters │
│                          │ improves generalization and parameter efficiency while keeping expressive three-qubit     │
│                          │ motifs aligned to the eight winning lines. The block preserves allowed gates and          │
│                          │ connectivity constraints.                                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
