│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ symmetry_motif_zzz_ccrz                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Key idea: reduce parameter count and inject geometry-aware high-order motifs aligned with │
│                          │ tic‑tac‑toe winning lines while preserving expressive entangling and local rotations. I   │
│                          │ restore a symmetry-grouped EfficientSU2-like layout that previously achieved stronger     │
│                          │ validation/test accuracy: (1) shared RY rotations per symmetry zone (corners, edges,      │
│                          │ center) to reduce redundant parameters, (2) CRZ entanglers around the outer ring with a   │
│                          │ separate shared center coupling to propagate radial correlations, (3) ZZZ three-qubit     │
│                          │ rotations explicitly placed on the eight winning lines so the circuit can directly form   │
│                          │ winning-line correlations, (4) two CCRZ patterns for compressed higher-order              │
│                          │ correlations, and (5) compact final rotations (shared RZ+RX per zone) to keep parameter   │
│                          │ count low but allow local phase flexibility.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should improve performance:                                                      │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency: sharing across symmetric qubits reduces N_PARAMS (to 78) which    │
│                          │ helps generalization and parameter_efficiency metric.                                     │
│                          │ - Motif alignment: placing ZZZ on the winning lines gives the optimizer direct primitives │
│                          │ to capture 3-body patterns crucial for the task, aiding accuracy and faster convergence.  │
│                          │ - Balanced entanglement: CRZ ring + center couplings spreads information across the grid  │
│                          │ without excessive distinct parameters, reducing train-test gap.                           │
│                          │ - Compact final rotations provide local flexibility without exploding parameter count.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All other training settings (Adam, re-uploading layout, feature map, n_uploads/n_repeats, │
│                          │ measurements) are unchanged to allow fair comparison.                                     │
