│ patch_description        │ This program is a crossover between two previous ANSATZ designs. It keeps the strong      │
│                          │ symmetry-based parametrization from the higher-performing candidate (shared RY across     │
│                          │ corners/edges/center, CRZ ring + center couplings, ZZZ motifs aligned with winning lines, │
│                          │ CCRZ high-order correlations, and compact final rotations) and adds a lightweight,        │
│                          │ symmetry-grouped pre-RZ layer (corners/edges/center). The pre-RZ layer increases          │
│                          │ single-qubit expressivity while remaining parameter-efficient by sharing across symmetry  │
│                          │ zones. All other parts of the original training and evaluation scaffolding are preserved  │
│                          │ (feature map, re-uploading, training loop, measurements, early stopping, etc.), and       │
│                          │ connectivity/parameter-sharing constraints are respected. The EVOLVE-BLOCK markers are    │
│                          │ preserved and only ANSATZ_SPEC is modified.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Keep the proven motif-aligned triples (ZZZ and CCRZ) which likely capture game-winning  │
│                          │ correlations.                                                                             │
│                          │ - Preserve CRZ shared entanglers for strong, parameter-efficient two-qubit coupling       │
│                          │ around the ring and to center.                                                            │
│                          │ - Add three shared pre-RZ parameters (corners, edges, center) to give richer local        │
│                          │ rotations before entangling, improving optimization without a large parameter cost.       │
│                          │ - Maintain compact final rotations shared by symmetry for readout tuning.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances expressivity and parameter efficiency to aim for improved validation/test   │
│                          │ performance and reduced generalization gap.                                               │
