│ patch_description        │ The current program uses Z-axis triple interactions (ZZZ) for all eight winning lines.    │
│                          │ This new candidate diversifies the interaction axes by alternating between ZZZ (MultiRZ)  │
│                          │ and CCRZ (doubly-controlled RZ) motifs across different geometric groups. Specifically,   │
│                          │ it applies ZZZ to the horizontal rows and diagonals, while utilizing CCRZ for the         │
│                          │ vertical columns to capture higher-order conditional correlations. Additionally, it       │
│                          │ introduces a 'mixing' layer of CNOTs on the grid edges to improve state distribution      │
│                          │ before the final symmetry-grouped RX/RZ rotations. This approach aims to increase the     │
│                          │ expressivity of the circuit by exploring different non-commuting basis interactions on    │
│                          │ the same winning-line motifs.                                                             │
