│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce passive CZ entanglement across all outer-ring and radial center edges (no extra │
│                          │ parameters), and add a single shared parametrized controlled-X (CRX) coupling from each   │
│                          │ edge to the center using one shared parameter "crx_center". The CZs give a fixed          │
│                          │ entangling scaffold that can help triple (ZZZ/CCRZ) motifs act on already-entangled       │
│                          │ subsystems without increasing parameter count; the shared CRX adds a lightweight,         │
│                          │ symmetry-respecting controllable non-commuting coupling to strengthen center-edge         │
│                          │ interactions while keeping parameter efficiency high. All two-qubit gates respect grid    │
│                          │ adjacency and we keep the winning-line ZZZ and CCRZ motifs plus compact symmetry-shared   │
│                          │ rotations. This aims to improve expressivity and training speed with minimal parameter    │
│                          │ overhead.                                                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
